    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0282" n="168" xml:id="pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4404</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lindsay</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-16">July 16, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In replying to your communication of
                    July 10, 1931, concerning the meeting in London on July 17 of financial experts,
                    I have to inform you that Mr. Hugh Gibson, American Ambassador at Brussels,
                    Belgium, will be the representative of this Government at the meeting in
                    question. His function, in view of the character of the discussions which will
                    take place, will be largely that of an observer.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R. Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
